INSERT INTO feature VALUES('exact-reals','algorithms','Exact real arithmetic beside the kernel',NULL,'partial','notable',NULL,'Canonical dyadics round to a chosen precision toward the floor or the ceiling and report whether they lost bits, and explicitly oriented intervals round outward under addition, subtraction, multiplication and division, held to a slow rational oracle. A computation over the reals is a plan: a DAG of real, open and domain nodes whose binders are de Bruijn indices, which holds each distinct subterm once and has one canonical byte form that the reader alone accepts and reads back to an equal plan. A total validation pass admits a plan only within its quotas, its binders in scope, its hulls proper and bounded and each evidence reference registered for its judgement, and it names the node and the check of a refusal. Dual approximation encloses each real node of a validated plan at a chosen precision and gives each comparison, meet and join a positive and a negative approximant, each sound on its own, so an undecided proposition is never reported false. A versioned certificate of primitive steps replays with exact dyadic arithmetic and comparison alone, within quotas, and the registered cut of the square root of two refines to a width of 2^-256 with one checked step per halving, a forged cut refused. The refinement machine of stage B runs typed obligations in bounded quanta within a budget, in a fixed order. A run writes a checkpoint that a later run resumes, and a cancellation stops it at the end of its quantum. The machine settles a bounded existential or universal over an interval by a witness or by a cover of the domain. A cache keyed by the canonical bytes of the plan that a node roots keeps the checked certificates, and the checker replays every hit before the machine uses it. Cut elimination rewrites a strict comparison that reads a cut on one side to the lower or the upper cut of that cut at the other side, so the machine encloses that side alone, and the certificate of the rewritten node replays on the comparison it replaces. No plan of field operations and cuts defines a transcendental real, so π, the cosine, the sine and the angle of a point are builtin nodes. Each builtin has one enclosure rule: an alternating series with outward rounding, whose next term bounds its remainder, at an absolute precision. A builtin step of a certificate states its precision, and the checker computes its conclusion by the same rule within the width quota. An enclosure at a finer precision lies inside the coarser one. A recurrence node is the sum of a series whose first term is one and whose term ratio is a rational function of the index. Its one rule sums a stated count of terms with outward rounding and adds a tail bound from the term ratio past them, after Johansson 2019, and validation refuses a ratio whose numerator has the higher degree or whose denominator vanishes at a natural number. `exp` and `log` are plans over the node with no rule of their own, and the generic rule encloses them within 1.25 times the time of a hand-written rule at 64, 256 and 1024 bits. A quotient or a power step rounds outward at its stated precision. The machine encloses a real made of constants, sums, differences, products, quotients, powers, the builtins and recurrences at a precision that doubles, and it decides a comparison of two such reals. Stage C opens the host interface `std.reals.Eff`. Its `admit` validates the canonical bytes of a plan in lowercase hexadecimal and replies a plan that the run holds. Its `enclose` replies the two ends of an enclosure of the root, and the checker replays the certificate before the reply. Its `decide` mints a machine on the two poles of an open root, such as `sqrt 2 < 3/2`, and runs it for a budget of quanta, one certificate step each. The verdict is `holds` or `fails` only with a certificate that the checker replays, and each other end is a named stop: `exhausted`, `suspended`, `pending` or `cancelled`. Its `step` runs one more quantum, its `checkpoint` spells an undecided machine with its plan, its `restore` validates that text again and mints a new machine, and its `report` gives nine counters: the quanta, the obligations and the certificate steps, then the frontier, the cache hits, the regions, the checker steps, the checkpoints and the cancellations. The host declines each refusal and names its cause on standard error. A profile of quotas, `default` or `bounded`, sets every quota of a run: `[reals] profile` in the configuration of `gandr run` names it, and an unknown profile stops the run before it starts. Through `gandr run`, a machine decides a bounded existential over an overt domain and a bounded universal over a compact domain. The host refuses a forged cut law, an escaped binder, a domain without its modality evidence and a false checkpoint, each by its check. A suspension, a cancellation or an exhausted budget never reads as false, and no real number enters the kernel. Stage C is the first release: at the median the host adds under 0.8 µs to an enclosure and under 0.2 µs to a decision over the crate alone.','theory-exact-reals core-term surface-dispatcher surface-driver','crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/oracle.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/dyadic.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/interval.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/plan.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/validate.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/approx.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/certificate.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/dovetail.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/checkpoint.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/quantifier.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/cache.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/elimination.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/elementary.rs crates/theory-exact-reals/tests/recurrence.rs corpus/model/reals/sqrt-two.gandr corpus/model/reals/comparison.gandr corpus/model/reals/boundary.gandr corpus/model/reals/resume.gandr corpus/model/reals/trigonometry.gandr corpus/model/reals/exponential.gandr corpus/model/reals/exists.gandr corpus/model/reals/forall.gandr corpus/model/reals/metrics.gandr corpus/pathological/reals/forged-cut-law.gandr corpus/pathological/reals/unscoped-binder.gandr corpus/pathological/reals/missing-compactness.gandr corpus/pathological/reals/false-checkpoint.gandr corpus/ledger/features/exact-reals.gandr crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/run.rs crates/surface-driver/tests/reals.rs','corpus/ledger/features/exact-reals.gandr','#638 #5345 #5346 #5347 #5348 #5354 #5700 #5703 #5786 #5705 #5704 #5851 #5852 #6013');
